---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';

// Linked from the app's Google Play and App Store listings. Keep this URL stable.
const contact = 'contact@itsvishalcodes.com';
---

<Base
  title="Retouched for LPU UMS privacy policy"
  description="How the Retouched for LPU UMS app for Android and iPhone handles your data: no backend, no ads, no analytics. Your UMS login goes only to the university’s servers."
>
  <article class="container-x max-w-3xl py-14 sm:py-20">
    <a href="/projects/lpu-retouched/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted transition-colors hover:text-ink">
      <Icon name="back" size={16} /> About the app
    </a>
    <h1 class="mt-8 text-4xl leading-[1.1] font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">Retouched for LPU UMS — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-sm text-subtle">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-13">13 October 2026</time></p>

    <div class="prose-case mt-10">
      <p>
        Retouched for LPU UMS (the “App”) is an independent, student-built client for Lovely Professional University’s UMS student
        portal. It is not an official app of, and is not endorsed by or affiliated with, the university. This policy explains what
        data the App handles and how.
      </p>

      <h2>Who processes your data</h2>
      <p>
        The App has <strong>no backend of its own</strong>. It is only a client: all data flows directly between your device and
        the university’s own servers (<code>ums.lpu.in</code>). The developer does not operate any server that receives, stores,
        or has access to your data, and does not sell your data.
      </p>

      <h2>What the App collects and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Login credentials (Registration/Unique ID and password).</strong> Entered by you and sent over an encrypted
          (HTTPS) connection to the university’s servers solely to sign you in. They are stored locally on your device so you stay
          signed in, and are removed when you log out or uninstall the App.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Device identifier.</strong> On Android the App uses the Android ID; on iPhone it uses Apple’s identifier for vendor
          (IDFV). It is sent to the university’s servers with your login and with the App’s other requests, for the university’s
          session and device handling, and is not sent anywhere else. It is not the advertising ID, and the App does not use it for
          tracking.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your academic information</strong> (attendance, marks, timetable, results, messages, announcements, profile and
          photo) is retrieved from the university’s servers and shown to you in the App. It is not sent anywhere else and is not
          collected by the developer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Photos you attach.</strong> When you attach a photo to a maintenance complaint, a duty-leave request or a
          parent-number ID proof, the App reads the photo you pick from your gallery and sends it only to the university’s servers
          with that request. It doesn’t keep a copy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Camera</h2>
      <p>
        The App uses the camera only to scan the QR codes for mess meals and hostel entry/exit. The camera image is read on your
        device; only the text inside the QR code is sent, together with the device identifier, to the university’s servers to
        record the meal or the entry/exit. The App takes no photos or videos and does not store or upload any camera images.
      </p>
      <p>
        The App asks for camera access the first time you scan. You can turn it off in your device’s settings, and everything
        except QR scanning keeps working.
      </p>

      <h2>What the App does NOT do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No advertising and no advertising ID.</li>
        <li>No third-party analytics or tracking SDKs.</li>
        <li>
          No sharing or selling of your data to any third party. Data is sent only to the university’s own servers to provide the
          service you request.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data security</h2>
      <p>All communication with the university’s servers uses HTTPS. Credentials cached on your device remain on your device.</p>

      <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Data stored by the App is limited to the login details cached on your device; clearing it is as simple as logging out or
        uninstalling the App. Your academic records are held by the university in its own systems — to access, correct, or delete
        those, contact the university directly.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The App is intended for enrolled university students and is not directed at children under 13.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>This policy may be updated; the “Last updated” date above will change accordingly.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
